Of course, a couple of buys is more than 2 AC on average.  And you pay
for it with a much more dangerous early game, in exchange for a
somewhat easier late early game.  I highly recommend doing a pacifist
PR several times until you know how to do it, but I really don't think
it's a good idea for consistent survivability--although BAJ's modified
racket where you level up a bit first and get some more hp makes it a
lot less dangerous.

But still, serial ascenders rarely do the PR for what seem like sound
reasons to me--the more sheer random deaths you can eliminate, the
more likely you are to succeed.  Those attack wands, rolling boulder
traps, etc are instadeaths at 15 HP but not 30; at 45 you might even
find a way to escape a gnome coming down a long corridor with /
lightning when you lack reflection.  Getting those HP puts events far
more in your control, and I find getting those HP (and PW, skill
slots, spell failure rates, etc) a couple thousand turns earlier a lot
more valuable than getting 6 AC a couple thousand turns earlier.



